	<!-- Welcome -->
	<string name="welcome_title">Welcome to Free eloquence TTS</string>
	<string name="welcome_alternative">The voice that reads to you, free, and yours to keep.</string>
	<string name="welcome_free">No payment, no account, no subscription, and nothing to sign in to. The whole engine is in this app.</string>
	<string name="welcome_intro">Everything is already working. This screen is what you get and the two permissions to allow; after it, the voice is yours.</string>
	<string name="welcome_features">What you get</string>
	<string name="welcome_voices">Nine voices</string>
	<string name="welcome_voices_description">Reed, Shelley, Bobby, Rocko, Glen, Sandy, Grandma, Grandpa and Luna. Every one of them can be tuned, and Luna is a clear female voice of her own.</string>
	<string name="welcome_languages">Eight languages</string>
	<string name="welcome_languages_description">American and British English, German, Spanish of Spain and of Mexico, French of France and of Canada, and Italian, each with all nine voices. Choose one as your own, let each app ask for the language of its page, or force your choice over every app.</string>
	<string name="welcome_web">Web pages, read properly</string>
	<string name="welcome_web_description">Links, headings, bold, italics, lists, quotes and images are announced as what they are instead of being read as flat text.</string>
	<string name="welcome_code">Code reading</string>
	<string name="welcome_code_description">Speaks camelCase, operators and indentation the way programmers hear them.</string>
	<string name="welcome_spelling">Spelling and symbols</string>
	<string name="welcome_spelling_description">Spells words out and reads punctuation, emoji and numbers on request.</string>
	<string name="welcome_dictionaries">Dictionaries that take anything</string>
	<string name="welcome_dictionaries_description">Teach the voice your names and abbreviations, and import word lists of any size — thousands or millions of words — without the voice ever going quiet.</string>
	<string name="welcome_permissions">Two permissions come next: notifications, and the exemption from battery optimization. The exemption is the one that keeps the voice alive when the phone is idle, so if you want the voice to work with the screen off, allow it. Nothing here is required to hear the voice today.</string>
	<string name="welcome_about">Everything on this screen can be changed later. The main screen has the settings, the dictionary, the audio and battery screens, and this welcome screen again.</string>
	<string name="welcome_codes">Numbers and one-time codes</string>
	<string name="welcome_codes_description">Long numbers can be read a digit, a pair or a triplet at a time, and a verification code in a message is read a digit at a time on its own — 4 9 2 8 0 1, never four hundred and ninety-two thousand.</string>
	<string name="welcome_routing">Sound where you want it</string>
	<string name="welcome_routing_description">By default every app plays its speech on the channel it chose. Synthesis routing can send everything to the accessibility channel, the media channel, or both.</string>
	<string name="welcome_continue">Get started</string>
	<string name="welcome_back_to_main">Back to the main screen</string>

