	<string name="section_text">Reading</string>
	<string name="number_mode_label">Numbers</string>
	<string name="number_mode_description">How a long number is spoken. Normal reads every number whole. The other three read a number of six or more digits a digit, a pair or a triplet at a time, from the left: 985256 becomes 9 8 5 2 5 6, 98 52 56 or 985 256. Shorter numbers, years, prices, decimals and numbers written with thousands separators are always read whole.</string>
	<string name="otp_label">Read one-time codes digit by digit</string>
	<string name="otp_description">A verification code in a message — \"your code is 492801\" — is read 4 9 2 8 0 1, whatever the number mode. The code is found from the words around it, in English, German, Spanish, French and Italian; years, prices, order numbers and telephone numbers are left alone.</string>
